Hello Fabbaloo team,

a release lead that may fit your coverage of the software side of AM.

Solidon3D takes downloaded 3D models and makes them editable without CAD
knowledge. Until now the result of an edit was always a triangle mesh: useful
for printing, useless for anyone who wanted to carry the part into a CAD
system.

Version 0.5.0 changes that. Primitives are built with real faces and edges,
and holes, slots, countersinks, bosses, beads, grooves and threads stay exact
when they are moved, duplicated, rotated or removed. STEP goes in and comes
back out cleanly. Two geometry kernels — a mesh kernel and an exact B-Rep
kernel — now run under one interface, and the four options that used to switch
between them have been removed. There is no kernel choice for the user any
more: Solidon keeps the exact body as long as it can, and says so when it
cannot. Existing projects keep computing unchanged.

What is worth noting is what is not claimed: Solidon does not reconstruct a
CAD model from arbitrary triangles. It recognises features, carries them
forward exactly where that is possible, and names the limit where it is not.
The provenance of every dimension is stated in the feature window — measured,
fitted, or taken from the construction step.

Further changes:

* A honeycomb pattern, knurl, set of ribs, waves or knobs is now one feature
  with pitch, cell width and depth instead of hundreds of faces, and can be
  removed or reapplied — including around a handle.
* Dimensions appear on the model with editable fields and a live preview.
* Resin printers are supported; exact bodies are meshed as finely as their
  pixels require, and the check report names the value.
* Recognition is several times faster, and moving a 200,000-triangle model
  answers in half a second instead of eight.

70 user-visible changes in this release, 896 since the first 0.1 demo.

Solidon3D is an independent development from Germany: desktop, one-time
purchase, fully usable offline after a single activation, no account, no
telemetry.

Solidon3D is a desktop application for Windows, macOS and Linux. One-time
purchase, no subscription, no account: after a single activation it runs fully
offline. Interface and manual are available in six languages, and there is a
demo.

I am happy to provide a review licence, print-resolution images or answers to
